    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-7",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "Test setup states 'manifest on disk is at 1.1.0 (== bump.to)' but never specifies the concrete bump.from and bump.to values. A developer writing the test from scratch cannot know whether bump.from is 1.0.0, 0.1.0, or any other value. The idempotent skip path is exercised only when current == bump.to; the choice of bump.from changes whether the from-branch code is even reachable, which affects what branch coverage the test exercises.",
      "suggested_fix": "Add explicit values to the test setup: 'bump.from = 1.0.0, bump.to = 1.1.0; manifest on disk is at 1.1.0 (== bump.to). A changeset file exists on disk.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-9",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "Test setup states 'manifest on disk is at 1.1.0 (== bump.to)' but like AC-7, does not specify bump.from or bump.to. Same gap: a developer writing the test cannot reconstruct the plan without guessing these values.",
      "suggested_fix": "Add: 'bump.from = 1.0.0, bump.to = 1.1.0; manifest on disk is at 1.1.0 (== bump.to). The changeset file does NOT exist on disk.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-4",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "'Propagating the existing filesystem or manifest-open error' does not specify how propagation occurs. Two valid implementations produce different concrete error types: (a) the ? operator with an existing From impl on GraphError yields the unwrapped variant; (b) map_err could wrap it into a new variant. GraphError already has #[from] Manifest impls but the spec does not say whether the propagation relies on those impls or adds a new wrapper.",
      "suggested_fix": "Rewrite: 'When a VersionWriteTarget::Manifest(p) does not exist on disk, apply_version_plan returns the Err produced by ManifestFormat::from_path or callisto_manifests::open via the ? operator, relying on the existing From impls on GraphError. No new error wrapping is introduced. The manifest is not created and no path for this bump is pushed to modified_paths.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-5",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "'Propagating the existing version-parse error from the manifest reader' has the same propagation ambiguity as AC-4. It is unclear whether ? with an existing From impl is used, or whether map_err introduces new wrapping.",
      "suggested_fix": "Rewrite: 'When the version field cannot be parsed as valid semver, apply_version_plan returns the Err produced by handle.version() via the ? operator, relying on the existing From impl for VersionParseError on GraphError. No new error variant is introduced for this case. The manifest is not modified and no path is pushed to modified_paths.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": null,
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "The relationship between the local variable modified_paths and ApplyOutcome::staged is never defined. AC-1 and AC-2 say 'pushed to modified_paths and appears in ApplyOutcome::staged' as though these are separate collections. In the real code (apply.rs line 321), outcome.staged = modified_paths — they are the same collection assigned at the end of the function. A developer could implement them as two separate Vec<PathBuf> values that must be kept in sync, or deduplicate one but not the other.",
      "suggested_fix": "Add a sentence to the scope or api_surface section: 'modified_paths is a local Vec<PathBuf> accumulator that is assigned to ApplyOutcome::staged verbatim at the end of apply_version_plan (outcome.staged = modified_paths). All criteria that say pushed to modified_paths and appears in ApplyOutcome::staged refer to this single collection.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": null,
      "type": "incomplete",
      "description": "api_surface.changes references line numbers 78-84 and 130-140. These are accurate today but will silently shift as the file grows (the three new tests added below line 327 have already made this a maintenance concern). A developer working from stale line numbers will edit the wrong location.",
      "suggested_fix": "Replace line numbers with structural anchors: 'In the VersionWriteTarget::Manifest arm of the write loop' and 'In the consumed_changesets loop.' The markers should be sufficient given the surrounding code is stable."
    }
  ],
  "overall": "fail",
  "reasoning": "Two issues are individually sufficient to fail the spec. First, AC-6 requires a developer to write a test verifying that a full.exists() guard is in place, but no observable assertion can verify the presence of a guard — this forces the implementer to either change the spec's meaning or write a test that inspects source. Second, AC-7 and AC-9 are underspecified test setups: without knowing bump.from and bump.to, two developers would independently produce non-equivalent tests. The propagation ambiguity in AC-4 and AC-5 is lower severity because the existing GraphError From impls make the intended mechanism inferrable from context, but it still admits a second valid interpretation. The modified_paths/staged relationship gap is a clarity defect that could produce a correct-but-divergent implementation. None of these are theoretical: each would cause a real developer to stop and ask a clarifying question."
}
```

