      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "\"matches packages from exactly two or more distinct ecosystems\" does not specify whether \"matches\" means (a) the PackageId::matches() predicate returns true for a package, or (b) that Bare rule is the governing rule for that package after specificity ordering (i.e., no Prefixed rule superseded it). When a Prefixed rule also matches cargo:foo and a Bare rule \"foo\" matches both cargo:foo and npm:foo, the Bare rule governs only npm:foo, yet its predicate matches both. Implementations (a) and (b) produce different diagnostic behavior for this case, and the criterion does not resolve the ambiguity.",
