  "scope": "Three changes: (1) the [[package]] rule lookup in ManifestWalkResolver::build in crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs, (2) a new cross-ecosystem diagnostic pass after the packages loop in the same function, (3) one new DiagnosticCode variant in crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs plus a corresponding row in the diagnostic registry table at docs/01-spec.md §G.13. PackageId::matches() is NOT changed. Packages map keys are always Bare PackageIds (the locator constructs ids from manifest name strings alone, which do not carry an ecosystem prefix). Ecosystem information for a given package is derived from the canonical ManifestDecl entries in the Package value — specifically ManifestDecl::ecosystem(), which delegates to ManifestFormat::ecosystem() and returns Ecosystem directly.",
  "non_goals": [
    "PackageId::matches() in identity.rs: bare-matches-all-ecosystems is correct and intentional. The fix is at the call site, not in the type.",
    "[[package-set]] rules: multi-ecosystem glob matching is their explicit purpose; they are exempt from the cross-ecosystem diagnostic.",
    "Specificity ordering among multiple Prefixed matches with different ecosystems: first-match-wins (declaration order) is correct for that case.",
    "Specificity ordering among multiple Bare matches: first-match-wins (declaration order) is unchanged.",
    "No new E-code is added: the diagnostic is a Warning, not a miette-diagnosed Error.",
    "Deduplication of identical PackageId entries in cfg.packages is out of scope; the diagnostic pass iterates the Vec as-is, so two identical Bare entries each produce their own diagnostic if both qualify.",
    "Bare-keyed packages map entries are excluded from the AC-5 distinct-ecosystem computation because key.ecosystem() returns None and contributes no Ecosystem value. Since the ProjectLocator always yields Prefixed ids this exclusion is a no-op in practice; the unreachable Bare-key case is out of scope for testing."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-1",
      "description": "When cfg.packages contains at least one Prefixed PackageId rule (ecosystem() is Some) that matches a given package P and at least one Bare PackageId rule (ecosystem() is None) that also matches that same package P, the first-matching Prefixed rule in declaration order has its PackageConfig applied to P (first-match-wins within the Prefixed tier), regardless of how many Bare rules also match P and regardless of their declaration order relative to the Prefixed rules.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-2",
      "description": "When the set of [[package]] rules in cfg.packages that match a given package consists entirely of Bare PackageId rules (no Prefixed rule in cfg.packages matches that package — other Prefixed rules matching different packages may still be present in the Vec), the first-matching Bare rule in declaration order is applied to that package.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-3",
      "description": "When the set of [[package]] rules in cfg.packages that match a given package consists entirely of Prefixed PackageId rules (no Bare rule in cfg.packages matches that package — other Bare rules that match different packages may still be present in the Vec), the first-matching Prefixed rule in declaration order is applied to that package.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4a",
      "description": "When no [[package]] rule in cfg.packages matches a given package but a [[package-set]] rule does match, the [[package-set]] rule's PackageConfig is returned for that package. When multiple [[package-set]] rules match, the first matching rule in cfg.package_sets declaration order is applied (first-match-wins).",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4b",
      "description": "When no [[package]] rule and no [[package-set]] rule matches a given package, None is returned for that package.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-5",
      "description": "After all packages have been discovered and inserted into the packages map (i.e., after the full packages loop in ManifestWalkResolver::build completes), for each Bare PackageId rule (pattern, _) in cfg.packages, compute the distinct-ecosystem set: the set of Ecosystem values E such that there exists an entry (key, _) in the packages map for which pattern.matches(key) returns true and key.ecosystem() == Some(E). If the distinct-ecosystem set has two or more elements, exactly one Diagnostic is pushed for that rule. N qualifying Bare rules (cfg.packages is iterated as-is, including duplicates) produce N diagnostics with code BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems. Among diagnostics filtered by code == BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems, the Nth such diagnostic corresponds to the Nth qualifying Bare rule in cfg.packages declaration order. Each diagnostic has: severity = Warning, code = DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems (new variant), package = None, path = None, escalated_by = None, governed_by = None, and a message containing the rule's pattern.name() string as a contiguous substring and, for each Ecosystem value E in the distinct-ecosystem set, E.prefix() (e.g. \"cargo\", \"npm\") as a contiguous substring. The message format is otherwise unconstrained. Example acceptable message: \"bare rule \\\"foo\\\" matches packages in multiple ecosystems: cargo, npm\".",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-6",
      "description": "When the distinct-ecosystem set computed per AC-5 for a Bare PackageId rule has fewer than two elements (zero or one), no Diagnostic with code BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems is pushed for that rule.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-7",
      "description": "Prefixed PackageId rules in cfg.packages never trigger a BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems diagnostic regardless of what they match.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-8",
      "description": "Rules in cfg.package_sets never trigger the cross-ecosystem diagnostic regardless of what they match.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-8b",
      "description": "The Diagnostic pushed per AC-5 has escalated_by = None and governed_by = None. The warning is advisory under --strict and --strict-graph; it does not escalate to a build failure in either strict mode.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-9a",
      "description": "When cfg.packages is empty, no BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems diagnostic is present in the resolver's diagnostics and the [[package]]-tier lookup returns None for every queried package. The [[package-set]]-tier fallback (AC-4a) continues to apply normally.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-9b",
      "description": "When cfg.packages is non-empty but the packages map contains zero entries (no packages discovered during the walk), no BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems diagnostic is present in the resolver's diagnostics, because the distinct-ecosystem set for every Bare rule is empty (no Prefixed-keyed entries in the map match anything).",
      "is_error_case": false
    }
  ],
  "api_surface": {
    "file": "crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs",
    "changes": [
      "Replace the cfg.packages.iter().find(...) call (the [[package]] lookup, ~line 154) with a two-pass search: first pass finds any Prefixed-pattern match (pattern.ecosystem().is_some()); second pass (only if first is None) finds any Bare-pattern match. Both passes use first-match-wins within their tier. Result is the same Option<&PackageConfig> type as before.",
      "After the packages loop (after packages.insert), add a pass over cfg.packages: for each (pattern, _) where pattern.ecosystem().is_none() (Bare), collect the distinct ecosystems of all packages in the just-built packages map whose id is matched by pattern. If the ecosystem count is > 1, push one Diagnostic { code: DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems, severity: DiagnosticSeverity::Warning, message: format!(...), package: None, path: None, escalated_by: None, governed_by: None }. Note: Diagnostic derives no Default — all seven fields must be written explicitly."
    ],
    "new_variants": [
      "DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems in crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs — add to the end of the DiagnosticCode enum, kebab-case serde name 'bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems'."
    ]
  }
}

